From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:27:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg: clear a lone CPU_INTERRUPT_EXITTB without the BQL

cpu_handle_interrupt() takes the BQL whenever interrupt_request is
non-zero.  Exception entries and returns that change the translation
state set only CPU_INTERRUPT_EXITTB (Arm on every exception it takes,
PowerPC on every rfi), so once delivery itself no longer needs the BQL
(TCGCPUOps.exception_bql_free) a system call still takes it once, here,
just to clear that bit.

When CPU_INTERRUPT_EXITTB is the only bit set, do what the locked path
does for it without the BQL: clear it (interrupt_request is atomic) and
forget the last TB so that it is not chained.  The locked path would
reach no other branch: no target's cpu_exec_interrupt acts on
CPU_INTERRUPT_EXITTB, record/replay logs nothing for it, and a bit set
concurrently stays set, its setter's kick bringing the loop back here.
Under record/replay the locked path is kept: in replay it consults the
log (replay_has_interrupt()) before anything else.

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Origin: new
---
 accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
index 62f5883a2b6828a0887d032562ecb95a53a8a293..0bb254b908d89d8e95835e6f2d1f04bd65ff7ae3 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
@@ -885,7 +885,20 @@ static inline bool cpu_handle_interrupt(CPUState *cpu,
 #ifdef CONFIG_USER_ONLY
     assert(!cpu_test_interrupt(cpu, ~0));
 #else
-    if (unlikely(cpu_test_interrupt(cpu, ~0))) {
+    if (qatomic_read(&cpu->interrupt_request) == CPU_INTERRUPT_EXITTB &&
+        replay_mode == REPLAY_MODE_NONE) {
+        /*
+         * Only a TB exit request (an exception entry or return that changed
+         * the translation state): what the locked path below does for it
+         * alone, without the BQL.  No target's cpu_exec_interrupt acts on
+         * CPU_INTERRUPT_EXITTB, interrupt_request is atomic, and a bit set
+         * concurrently stays set (the setter's kick makes the next TB exit
+         * and brings us back here).  Record/replay keeps the locked path,
+         * which consults the replay log.
+         */
+        cpu_reset_interrupt(cpu, CPU_INTERRUPT_EXITTB);
+        *last_tb = NULL;
+    } else if (unlikely(cpu_test_interrupt(cpu, ~0))) {
         bql_lock();
         if (cpu_test_interrupt(cpu, CPU_INTERRUPT_DEBUG)) {
             cpu_reset_interrupt(cpu, CPU_INTERRUPT_DEBUG);
